      "state": {
        "ringSize": 9,
        "strainRegions": "Off"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Large rings relax",
      "narration": "By 12 and 13 strain falls off, and at 14 it is zero again: large rings are floppy enough to adopt strain-free conformations like extended alkane chains.",
      "state": {
        "ringSize": 14,
        "strainRegions": "Off"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Four regimes, one picture",
      "narration": "Turn on the region shading: small (3–4), common (5–7), medium (8–13), and large (14+). The irregular bar heights are really four different physical causes of strain acting in different size ranges.",
      "state": {
        "ringSize": 14,
        "strainRegions": "Small / Common / Medium / Large"
      }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "Ring strain does not decrease smoothly as rings get bigger — it collapses to zero at cyclohexane, rebounds in the medium rings because of transannular crowding, and only vanishes again once the ring is large enough to behave like an open chain.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Recreate as a Chart.js vertical bar chart: pale blue (#e8f4fb) plot area, medium-blue bars (#1a75bc) with thin darker outlines, white page background, black axis text. Left axis 'Strain energy (kJ/mol)' 0–120 step 20 with light gray horizontal gridlines; right axis '(kcal/mol)' 0–28.7 with ticks 0, 4.8, 9.6, 14.3, 19.1, 23.9 (same physical scale, 1 kcal = 4.184 kJ). X-axis 'Ring size' ticks 3–14, bars at all positions except 6 and 14, where a short thin black downward arrow tipped at the baseline carries a '0' label above it. Bar silhouette must read: two very tall bars at 3 and 4, sharp drop to short bars at 5 and 7, a rising hump 8→9 peaking ~53, gentle decline 10, 11, a low bar at 12, a modest bar at 13. Selected bar (slider) turns a saturated highlight color (e.g. orange #e8730c) with a floating readout box giving 'n = X · YY kJ/mol · ZZ kcal/mol'; non-selected bars dim slightly. Clicking a zero marker at 6 or 14 thickens and reddens the arrow, pulses the '0', and dims all bars except the immediate neighbors so the contrast with adjacent strained rings stays visible. Region toggle overlays four translucent vertical bands behind the bars with small top labels: 'Small (angle strain)', 'Common', 'Medium (transannular)', 'Large'."
}

